1.Download the Repository:
Get the extension source files to your local machine.
Click the green Code button on the GitHub repository page.
Select Download ZIP and extract the folder to a convenient location on your computer.(Alternatively, if you use Git, run git clone <repository-url> in your terminal.)
2.Enable Developer Mode in Chrome:
Prerequisite for loading unpacked extensions.
Open Google Chrome and navigate to chrome://extensions in the address bar.
In the top-right corner, toggle the Developer mode switch to ON.
3.Load the Unpacked Extension:
Inject the Manifest V3 extension into Chrome.
Click the Load unpacked button that appears in the top-left toolbar.
Select the extracted project folder (the directory containing the manifest.json file).
PhishShield AI will now appear in your list of extensions and install to your browser toolbar.
